# Copy to .env (git-ignored) at the repository root. `make start` and `make url` pass it to
# the backend with --env-file. Lines are KEY=VALUE, with an optional `export`, optional quotes
# and `#` comments.
#
# The backend reads one variable from this file:
#
#   CWBCODE_WALLET   the public address (0x and 40 hex digits) of the wallet that owns the
#                    backend. Set, it turns remote mode on: the backend listens on 0.0.0.0:7443
#                    and asks for a sign-in with that wallet. Empty or absent: local mode,
#                    127.0.0.1:7443, no login. A value set in the environment wins over this
#                    file; one fixed here is not changed from the dashboard. Only the public
#                    address belongs here: a private key or a recovery phrase is refused.
CWBCODE_WALLET=

# The rest are read from the process environment only, not from this file:
#
#   backend (cwbcode)
#     CWBCODE_HOME          where it keeps its database, certificate, token, tools [~/.cwbcode]
#     CWBCODE_BIND          the address to listen on, as --bind (make start BIND=addr:port)
#     CWBCODE_PORT          the port when no address is given [7443]
#     CWBCODE_MODEL         the model, by its name in Ollama's store [inkling-2-mini:26b-a5b-nvfp4]
#     CWBCODE_MODELS        where a model downloaded from Hugging Face is kept [~/.cwbcode/models]
#     OLLAMA_MODELS         Ollama's store [~/.ollama/models]
#     CWBCODE_MLX_CACHE_GB  MLX's buffer cache limit in GB [2]
#     INKLING_DRAFT=0       turn speculative decoding off; INKLING_STATS, INKLING_TRACE,
#                           INKLING_DEPTH, INKLING_CHUNK, INKLING_ROWS, INKLING_IMAGE_SIDE and
#                           INKLING_F32_PRODUCTS are for measuring and debugging the model
#
#   terminal client (cwbcodeclient)
#     CWBCODE_SERVER        the backend's address [https://127.0.0.1:7443]
#     CWBCODE_CERT          the backend's certificate, the only one trusted [~/.cwbcode/cert.pem]
#     CWBCODE_HOME          as above
#     NO_COLOR              no colours
#
#   model download (rust/scripts/model.py)
#     CWBCODE_MODEL, CWBCODE_MODELS, OLLAMA_MODELS as above; OLLAMA_HOST [127.0.0.1:11434]
#     HF_TOKEN (or HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN, HF_TOKEN_PATH, HF_HOME): a Hugging Face token, used
#                           when there is one; none is needed
#
# Never put these in this file: they are secrets, and the backend does not read them from it.
#   CWBCODE_PHRASE        a recovery phrase for `cwbcodeclient login` / `remote on`
#   CWBCODE_TOKEN         a session or the backend's token for the client
